error[E0911]: the macro `make_enum` splices `#{m} + 1` where an enum member goes
  --> tests/ui/macro_enum_fragment.wid:19:1
   |
19 | make_enum :Color, :Green, :Blue
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `make_enum` expands here
  ::: tests/ui/macro_enum_fragment.wid:8:7
   |
 8 |       #{m} + 1
   |       -------- this line is neither a member nor a declaration
...
14 |       #{lines}
   |       -------- it is spliced here, among an enum's members
help: each line spliced among an enum's members is a member, written as a name alone (`#{name}`) or `name = value`, or a declaration such as a `def`
   = see `wid explain E0911`

error[E0913]: a macro can't add members to `Shade`
  --> tests/ui/macro_enum_fragment.wid:25:5
   |
25 |     Yellow
   |     ^^^^^^ `more_members` generates the member `Yellow`
  ::: tests/ui/macro_enum_fragment.wid:33:7
   |
33 |       more_members()
   |       -------------- `more_members` expands here
  ::: tests/ui/macro_enum_fragment.wid:38:1
   |
38 | with_more :Shade
   | ---------------- `with_more` expands here
   = note: an enum's members are fixed before the macros in its body run, so a macro can't add members
help: splice the members into the generated `enum` itself: names alone or `Name = value`, alone on a line in its body
   = see `wid explain E0913`

error: could not compile due to 2 errors
